          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: उल्का",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उल्का — ulkā — \"a shooting star; a meteor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रात्रौ आकाशे उल्का पतति। rātrau ākāśe ulkā patati. At night a shooting star falls across the sky."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उल्का (ulkā) comes from the root √uṣ, \"to burn\", to which MW refers it; MW gives ulkā as a fiery phenomenon in the sky, a meteor, a firebrand (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
